lled shape retained after recorded evidence shows every natural loop form fails.\n        </description>\n        <canonical_example id=\"natural-loop-pointer-stride\" severity=\"pre_ship_review\">\n            <bad_code>if (count != 0) {\n    cur = groups;\n    do {\n        HSD_SynthSFXGroupDataReaddress(cur);\n        cur++;\n        count--;\n    } while (count != 0);\n}</bad_code>\n            <preferred_code>for (i = 0; i &lt; count; i++) {\n    HSD_SynthSFXGroupDataReaddress(&amp;groups[i]);\n}\n/* Keep the source loop zero-or-more and indexable when the array count is known. */</preferred_code>\n            <why>\n                - A guarded pointer-walk can be decompiler residue for an ordinary counted loop.\n                - The counted loop exposes the authored array shape and avoids preserving control flow solely because it currently matches.\n            </why>\n        </canonical_example>\n        <qa_rules>\n            - m2c_goto_label\n            - m2c_residue_names\n        </qa_rules>\n    </standard>\n    <standard id=\"infer-authored-source-style\">\n        <description>\n            - Matching is required to reconstruct the likely original authored source, not arbitrary C that moves a score; a shape that only moves a score is rejected.\n            - Matched siblings, nearby files, headers, macros, naming habits, control-flow idioms, and review evidence are required inputs for inferring the original developers' local standards before any generated, permuter-shaped, or data-driven source is retained.\n        </description>\n        <canonical_example id=\"authored-style-local-inline-count\" severity=\"pre_ship_review\">\n            <bad_code>PAD_STACK(8);\ncount = 0;\nif (mnEvent_8024D1E4(0) != 0) count++;\nif (mnEvent_8024D1E4(1) != 0) count++;\nif (mnEvent_8024D1E4(2) != 0) count++;</bad_code>\n            <preferred_code>static inline s32 mnEvent_CountUnlocked(void)\n{\n    s32 i;\n    s32 count = 0;\n\n    for (i = 0; i &lt; 3; i++) {\n        if (mnEvent_8024D1E4(i) != 0) {\n            count++;\n        }\n    }\n    return count;\n}\n\ncount = mnEvent_CountUnlocked();</preferred_code>\n            <why>\n                - Local sibling helpers are stronger source-shape evidence than stack padding plus repeated generated calls.\n                - Restore the authored helper boundary when nearby code shows the project used that boundary.\n            </why>\n        </canonical_example>\n    </standard>\n    <standard id=\"typed-fields-over-pointer-math\">\n        <description>\n            - When a type can describe an access, real fields, correct FighterVars/GroundVars/ItemVars union arms, accessors, or temporary internal structs are required; M2C_FIELD and raw pointer arithmetic may not ship in accepted source.\n            - The single permitted exception is a type_erasing_cast surfaced for llm_review, which must be justified in the attempt summary; a raw ((u8*) obj) + offset access without that review is rejected.\n        </description>\n        <canonical_example id=\"typed-item-vars-owning-base\" qa_rule_id=\"pointer_offset_arithmetic\" severity=\"warning\">\n            <bad_code>Item* ip = GET_ITEM(gobj);\nvalue = *(s32*) ((u8*) ip + 0xE38);</bad_code>\n            <preferred_code>typedef struct itArwingLaser_ItemVars {\n    char x0_pad[0x64];\n    s32 xE38;\n} itArwingLaser_ItemVars;\n\nvalue = ip-&gt;xDD4_itemVar.arwinglaser.xE38;</preferred_code>\n            <why>\n                - Recover item-var fields from the owning Item.xDD4 base, not from the first offset that happens to be used.\n                - The typed union arm documents ownership and keeps later offsets from drifting.\n            </why>\n        </canonical_example>\n        <qa_rules>\n            - stage_ground_var_owner\n            - m2c_field_use\n            - type_erasing_cast\n            - pointer_offset_arithmetic\n        </qa_rules>\n    </standard>\n    <standard id=\"header-inlines\">\n        <description>\n            - Expanded header asserts, especially from jobj.h, must be mapped back to the existing inline/helper when line numbers and local evidence identify the source-level operation; keeping the expanded body is rejected.\n            - Local helper boundaries must be restored when duplicated expanded bodies or sibling functions show an authored helper shape.\n        </description>\n        <canonical_example id=\"header-inline-jobj-helper\" qa_rule_id=\"copied_jobj_inline\" severity=\"error\">\n            <bad_code>static inline void LocalSetMtxDirty(HSD_JObj* jobj)\n{\n    if (jobj == NULL) {\n        __assert(\"jobj.h\", 0x2F4, \"jobj\");\n    }\n    jobj-&gt;flags |= JOBJ_MTX_DIRTY;\n}</bad_code>\n            <preferred_code>HSD_JObjSetMtxDirty(jobj);\n/* Or use the shared WithMtxDirty variant when that is the evidenced helper. */</preferred_code>\n            <why>\n                - Local fake helpers that mirror jobj.h asserts and writes should be compared against the owning header helper.\n                - The fix path is to recover the canonical helper rather than copy the inline body into each TU.\n            </why>\n        </canonical_example>\n        <qa_rules>\n            - copied_jobj_inline\n            - unrolled_assert\n        </qa_rules>\n    </standard>\n    <standard id=\"assert-report-macros\">\n        <description>\n            - Raw assert/report expansions must become HSD_ASSERT, HSD_ASSERTMSG, HSD_ASSERTREPORT, OSReport, or OSPanic forms whenever the file, line, message, and side effects match local project idioms; a shipped raw __assert block that had a macro form is rejected.\n            - There is no exception: an existing macro form must replace the raw expansion, and real report/panic side effects may not be dropped.\n        </description>\n        <canonical_example id=\"assert-report-direct-asserts\" qa_rule_id=\"unrolled_assert\" severity=\"error\">\n            <bad_code>if (obj == NULL) {\n    __assert(__FIL